// ModelSwapper cvars.
server bool rs_foreignmodels         = true;   // master switch
server bool rs_foreignmodels_dump    = false;  // dump the scan to console
server bool rs_foreignmodels_showall = false;  // include weapons with no slot binding

// (rs_foreignmodels_natural and rs_fm_learned are gone: the remap engine
// reads timing off the weapon's own state table every tic, so there is
// no learned timing to store and no "natural rate" distinct from theirs.
// A stale archived copy in an old ini is ignored harmlessly.)

// The player's own model choices, packed as class:archetype:pick1:pick2;...
// Written every time a pick changes. Keyed on class name only -- no notion
// of "which mod" anywhere -- which is what makes this work as a per-mod
// profile with nothing tracking which mod is loaded: only one mod's classes
// exist in the world at a time. Clear it with the menu.
server string rs_fm_picks = "";

// A muzzle flash is a separate psprite layer, so it stays the mod's flat
// sprite even when the gun beside it is one of our models -- which reads as a
// billboard hanging in the air in VR. On by default; off renders the mod
// exactly as its author drew it.
server bool rs_fm_hideflash       = true;
// Opacity used when the above is on. 0.0 = fully invisible, which is the
// point of the option; raise it to keep a dimmed flash for the shot feedback
// without the full-screen billboard.
server float rs_fm_flashalpha     = 0.0;

// Hitscan -> projectile conversion. Off by default, and the only setting
// here that changes how the loaded mod plays rather than how it looks.
server bool rs_fm_ballistic       = false;  // player hitscans become travelling rounds
// 300, not 90, for two reasons that happen to agree.
//
// GunBonsai infers whether a weapon is a hitscan or a projectile weapon from
// the speed of what it fires, and counts anything at 300 map units per tic or
// faster as a hitscan -- a threshold it added for mods that simulate bullets
// with fast projectiles, which is exactly what this is. Below it, every
// converted shotgun and rifle is filed as a projectile weapon and offered the
// wrong upgrade tree. It also credits XP to the weapon held when the round
// LANDS, so a shorter flight time is a smaller window to fire, swap, and have
// the XP go to the wrong gun.
//
// It is also the fastest the trail can draw at full density: one bit per 12
// units, 24 per tic, so 300 units of travel is 25 requested against 24 allowed.
// Faster than this and the streak starts to gap.
server int  rs_fm_ballistic_speed = 300;    // map units per tic, clamped 10-400

// Bullet Time X compensation. Inert unless that mod is loaded alongside.
// 0.0 = player as slow as the monsters, 1.0 = normal player movement speed
// -- their own player-divisor cvar has no faster setting than that, so 1.0
// is the true ceiling, not a compromise. Default 0.0 because Bullet Time X
// itself ships with the player divisor equal to the world divisor -- 0.0 IS
// their own out-of-the-box behavior, so enabling this changes nothing until
// the slider actually moves.
server bool   rs_fm_bt       = false;
server float  rs_fm_bt_scale = 0.0;
// Their player-movement divisors as they were before we touched them,
// packed "normal:dodge:berserk:berserkdodge". Kept in a cvar so quitting
// with compensation on cannot strand their settings overwritten.
server string rs_fm_bt_base  = "";

// Extra distance from the grip to the muzzle, on top of the per-family
// figure. The engine has no muzzle concept -- shots start at the hand.
server int rs_fm_muzzle = 0;   // map units, clamped -20..80

// Collapse the picker to ONE ROW PER FAMILY. For arsenal mods that build
// weapons combinatorially (DoomRL Arsenal's ~150 assemblies), where every
// row is technically a distinct class but the menu is unusable. Off by
// default: on a normal mod each weapon deserves its own row.
server bool rs_foreignmodels_byfamily = false;
